r of Features       : 25\n","\n"," FINAL TEST RESULTS (MITIGATED)\n","-----------------------------------\n","AUC Score    : 0.9168\n","F1-Score     : 0.6996\n","Recall       : 0.6965\n","Precision    : 0.7028\n","\n"," FAIRNESS IMPACT\n","-----------------------------------\n","AUC Delta vs Baseline : -0.0033\n","F1 Delta vs Baseline  : +0.0190\n","\n","======================================================================\n","PHASE 4 — SAVING ALL ARTIFACTS\n","======================================================================\n","  Experiment log (full)   → /content/experiment_log_full.json\n","  Feature registry (full) → /content/feature_registry_full.csv\n","  Fairness report         → /content/fairness_report.csv\n","  Pipeline summary (full) → /content/pipeline_summary_full.md\n"]},{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"],"text/markdown":""},"metadata":{}}],"source":["# Project: FeatureBot - AI-Guided Feature Engineering for UCI Adult Income\n","# Tools: Google Colab, Python (pandas, scikit-learn)\n","# Skills: Feature Engineering, Prompting(chatgpt,gemini )\n","# Install libraries if needed (Colab usually has these pre-installed)\n","!pip install category_encoders\n","import numpy as np\n","import pandas as pd\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold, cross_val_score, cross_validate\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder, StandardScaler\n","from sklearn.pipeline import Pipeline\n","from sklearn.impute import SimpleImputer\n","from sklearn.compose import ColumnTransformer\n","from sklearn.linear_model import LogisticRegression\n","from sklearn.metrics import roc_auc_score, precision_recall_fscore_support, classification_report\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","import category_encoders as ce\n","import time\n","from datetime  import datetime\n","import  json\n","import warnings\n","warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')\n","\n","from sklearn.metrics import (\n","    roc_auc_score, f1_score, precision_score, recall_score,\n","    classification_report, confusion_matrix,\n","    precision_recall_fscore_support, roc_curve\n",")\n","from sklearn.calibration import CalibratedClassifierCV\n","from sklearn.ensemble import GradientBoostingClassifier\n","\n","# Load the data\n","\n","from google.colab import files\n","files.upload()\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# 0. FETCH DATA\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","COLUMN_NAMES = [\n","    \"age\", \"workclass\", \"fnlwgt\", \"education\", \"educational_num\",\n","    \"marital_status\", \"occupation\", \"relationship\", \"race\", \"sex\",\n","    \"capital_gain\", \"capital_loss\", \"hours_per_week\", \"native_country\", \"income\"\n","]\n","\n","\n","df = pd.read_csv('/content/Adult_income.csv', sep=',', on_bad_lines='skip')\n","display(df.head())\n","#df = pd.read_csv('/content/Adult_income.csv')\n","df.columns = [c.strip().lower().replace(\"-\", \"_\") for c in df.columns]\n","df = df.replace('?', np.nan) # \"?\" to nan for missing\n","\n","# identify columns that are not duplicate\n","df = df.loc[:, ~df.columns.duplicated()]\n","#return the total no of duplicate rows\n","df.duplicated().sum()\n","#drop the duplicate rows\n","df = df.drop_duplicates()\n","\n","if 'income' in df:\n","    df['income'] = df['income'].astype(str).str.strip().replace({'>50K.': '>50K', '<=50K.': '<=50K'})\n","    df['income'] = df['income'].map({'>50K': 1, '<=50K': 0})\n","    print(df.head())\n","    print(\"\\nMissing Counts:\\n\", df.isnull().sum())\n","    print(\"\\nClass Balance:\\n\", df['income'].value_counts(normalize=True))\n","    df.describe(include='all').T\n","\n","\n","# Numeric distributions\n","df.select_dtypes(include='number').hist(figsize=(15,8), bins=30)\n","plt.suptitle(\"Numeric Distributions\")\n","plt.show()\n","\n","# Value counts for categoricals\n","for col in df.select_dtypes('object').columns:\n","    print(f\"\\n{col} value counts:\\n\", df[col].value_counts(dropna=False)[:10])\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# TEMPLATE A: SCHEMA\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"TEMPLATE A — SCHEMA\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","SCHEMA = {\n","    \"target\": \"income\",\n","    \"target_encoding\": {\">50K\": 1, \"<=50K\": 0, \">50K.\": 1, \"<=50K.\": 0},\n","    \"drop_columns\": [\"fnlwgt\"],          # EXCLUDED per requirement\n","    \"numeric_features\": [\"age\", \"educational_num\", \"capital_gain\", \"capital_loss\", \"hours_per_week\"],\n","    \"categorical_features\": [\"workclass\", \"education\", \"marital_status\", \"occupation\",\n","                              \"relationship\", \"race\", \"sex\", \"native_country\"],\n","    \"missing_strategy\": \"mode_for_cat__median_for_num\",\n","    \"notes\": \"fnlwgt is a census weighting artifact — excluded to prevent spurious correlations.\"\n","}\n","\n","print(\"\\nSCHEMA:\")\n","for k, v in SCHEMA.items():\n","    print(f\"  {k:<25s}: {v}\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# TEMPLATE A: EDA HIGHLIGHTS (Adjusted to use df_modeling consistently)\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"TEMPLATE A — EDA HIGHLIGHTS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# Create df_modeling here, after initial cleaning and target setup\n","df_modeling = df.copy()\n","\n","# Drop fnlwgt immediately from df_modeling as per SCHEMA and EDA block intention\n","if \"fnlwgt\" in df_modeling.columns:\n","    df_modeling.drop(columns=[\"fnlwgt\"], inplace=True)\n","\n","# The 'income' column is already numeric (0/1) and is our target.\n","# The SCHEMA['target'] is 'income'. So, df_modeling already has its target set.\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Shape (after fnlwgt drop): {df_modeling.shape}\")\n","print(f\"  Target distribution     : {df_modeling[SCHEMA['target']].value_counts().to_dict()}\")\n","print(f\"  Class imbalance ratio   : {df_modeling[SCHEMA['target']].mean():.3f} (fraction >50K)\")\n","\n","# Missing values\n","missing = df_modeling.isnull().sum()\n","missing = missing[missing > 0]\n","print(f\"\\n  Missing values:\")\n","if len(missing) == 0:\n","    print(\"    None detected.\")\n","else:\n","    for col, cnt in missing.items():\n","        print(f\"    {col}: {cnt} ({cnt/len(df_modeling)*100:.1f}%)\") # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Numeric stats\n","print(\"\\n  Numeric feature stats (mean | std | skew):\")\n","for col in SCHEMA[\"numeric_features\"]:\n","    if col in df_modeling.columns:\n","        print(f\"    {col:<20s}: mean={df_modeling[col].mean():.1f}, std={df_modeling[col].std():.1f}, skew={df_modeling[col].skew():.2f}\")\n","\n","# Capital gain/loss zero rate\n","print(f\"\\n  Capital gain == 0 : {(df_modeling['capital_gain']==0).mean()*100:.1f}%\")\n","print(f\"  Capital loss == 0 : {(df_modeling['capital_loss']==0).mean()*100:.1f}%\")\n","print(f\"  Hours per week >60: {(df_modeling['hours_per_week']>60).mean()*100:.1f}%\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# TEMPLATE A: BASELINE ERRORS\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"TEMPLATE A — BASELINE MODEL ERRORS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","from sklearn.preprocessing import LabelEncoder\n","def prepare_baseline(df_in):\n","    \"\"\"Minimal preprocessing for baseline.\"\"\"\n","    df_ = df_in.copy()\n","    # Fill missing\n","    for col in SCHEMA[\"categorical_features\"]:\n","        if col in df_.columns:\n","            df_[col].fillna(df_[col].mode()[0], inplace=True)\n","    for col in SCHEMA[\"numeric_features\"]:\n","        if col in df_.columns:\n","            df_[col].fillna(df_[col].median(), inplace=True)\n","    # Label encode cats\n","    for col in SCHEMA[\"categorical_features\"]:\n","        if col in df_.columns:\n","            le = LabelEncoder()\n","            df_[col] = le.fit_transform(df_[col].astype(str))\n","    return df_\n","\n","df_base = prepare_baseline(df_modeling) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","feat_cols = SCHEMA[\"numeric_features\"] + SCHEMA[\"categorical_features\"]\n","feat_cols = [c for c in feat_cols if c in df_base.columns]\n","\n","X_base = df_base[feat_cols].values\n","y = df_base[SCHEMA[\"target\"]].values # Changed \"target\" to SCHEMA[\"target\"]\n","\n","skf = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n","\n","baseline_model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","bl_auc = cross_val_score(baseline_model, X_base, y, cv=skf, scoring=\"roc_auc\")\n","bl_f1  = cross_val_score(baseline_model, X_base, y, cv=skf, scoring=\"f1\")\n","\n","BASELINE_RESULTS = {\n","    \"auc_mean\": bl_auc.mean(), \"auc_std\": bl_auc.std(),\n","    \"f1_mean\":  bl_f1.mean(),  \"f1_std\":  bl_f1.std(),\n","    \"n_features\": len(feat_cols)\n","}\n","print(f\"\\n  Baseline AUC : {bl_auc.mean():.4f} ± {bl_auc.std():.4f}\")\n","print(f\"  Baseline F1  : {bl_f1.mean():.4f} ± {bl_f1.std():.4f}\")\n","print(f\"  Feature count: {len(feat_cols)}\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# FEATURE PROPOSALS WITH LEAKAGE CHECKS\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"FEATURE PROPOSALS — ≥5 PROPOSALS WITH LEAKAGE CHECKS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","FEATURE_PROPOSALS = [\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F1\",\n","        \"name\": \"age_bins\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binning\",\n","        \"description\": \"Bin age into 5 life-stage groups: Teen(17-24), Young Adult(25-34), Mid-Career(35-49), Senior(50-64), Elder(65+)\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — age is recorded at census time, no future info.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"HIGH — captures nonlinear income curve peaking at mid-career.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_AGE_BINS\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F2\",\n","        \"name\": \"capital_net\",\n","        \"type\": \"Interaction / Arithmetic\",\n","        \"description\": \"capital_net = capital_gain - capital_loss; captures overall investment outcome\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — both capital features are pre-survey; no target info used.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"HIGH — consolidates two sparse features; investors earn >50K.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F3\",\n","        \"name\": \"has_capital_activity\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binary Indicator\",\n","        \"description\": \"Flag = 1 if capital_gain > 0 OR capital_loss > 0 (investor proxy)\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — purely derived from input features at collection time.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — >90% zeros in capital; this flag separates investor group.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F4\",\n","        \"name\": \"hours_category\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binning + Encoding\",\n","        \"description\": \"Categorize hours_per_week: Part-time(<35), Standard(35-45), Overtime(46-60), Extreme(>60)\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — hours are self-reported at survey time.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — overtime/extreme workers more likely >50K.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F5\",\n","        \"name\": \"edu_hours_interaction\",\n","        \"type\": \"Multiplicative Interaction\",\n","        \"description\": \"edu_hours = educational_num * hours_per_week — high-edu high-hours signals professional\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — both inputs are survey-time features with no target leakage.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM-HIGH — captures synergistic effect between education and effort.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_EDU_HOURS\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F6\",\n","        \"name\": \"marital_binary\",\n","        \"type\": \"Encoding Simplification\",\n","        \"description\": \"Collapse marital_status to is_married (1 if Married-civ-spouse or Married-AF-spouse, else 0)\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — marital status is not derived from income.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — married individuals significantly more likely >50K in this dataset.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"F7\",\n","        \"name\": \"high_edu_flag\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binary Indicator from Binning\",\n","        \"description\": \"is_high_edu = 1 if educational_num >= 13 (Bachelors or above)\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — education is an input feature with no target dependency.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — higher education strongly correlated with >50K income.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\"\n","    },\n","]\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Total proposals: {len(FEATURE_PROPOSALS)}\")\n","print(f\"\\n  {'ID':<4} {'Name':<28} {'Type':<28} {'Leakage':<8} {'Toggle'}\")\n","print(\"  \" + \"-\"*95)\n","for p in FEATURE_PROPOSALS:\n","    status = \"✓ PASS\" if \"PASS\" in p[\"leakage_check\"] else \"✗ FAIL\"\n","    print(f\"  {p['id']:<4} {p['name']:<28} {p['type']:<28} {status:<8} {p['toggle']}\")\n","\n","print(\"\\n  All features PASS leakage check — no future data, no target-derived statistics.\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# add_feature_block WITH TOGGLES\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"add_feature_block — IMPLEMENTATION WITH TOGGLES\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","def add_feature_block(df_in, toggles=None):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Add engineered features to the dataframe.\n","\n","    Parameters\n","    ----------\n","    df_in : pd.DataFrame\n","        Preprocessed dataframe (fnlwgt already excluded).\n","    toggles : dict\n","        Feature toggles. Each key maps to True/False.\n","        Defaults: all features ON.\n","\n","    Returns\n","    -------\n","    df_out : pd.DataFrame\n","        Dataframe with added feature columns.\n","    new_features : list\n","        Names of added feature columns.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    DEFAULT_TOGGLES = {\n","        \"USE_AGE_BINS\":       True,\n","        \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\":    True,\n","        \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\":   True,\n","        \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True,\n","        \"USE_EDU_HOURS\":      True,\n","        \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True,\n","        \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\":  True,\n","    }\n","    if toggles is None:\n","        toggles = DEFAULT_TOGGLES\n","    else:\n","        toggles = {**DEFAULT_TOGGLES, **toggles}\n","\n","    df_out = df_in.copy()\n","    new_features = []\n","\n","    # F1 — Age bins (life-stage encoding)\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_AGE_BINS\", True):\n","        bins   = [0, 24, 34, 49, 64, 120]\n","        labels = [0, 1, 2, 3, 4]          # ordinal life stage\n","        df_out[\"age_bins\"] = pd.cut(df_out[\"age\"], bins=bins, labels=labels).astype(float)\n","        new_features.append(\"age_bins\")\n","\n","    # F2 — Net capital (gain - loss)\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_CAPITAL_NET\", True):\n","        df_out[\"capital_net\"] = df_out[\"capital_gain\"] - df_out[\"capital_loss\"]\n","        new_features.append(\"capital_net\")\n","\n","    # F3 — Binary capital activity flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\", True):\n","        df_out[\"has_capital_activity\"] = (\n","            (df_out[\"capital_gain\"] > 0) | (df_out[\"capital_loss\"] > 0)\n","        ).astype(int)\n","        new_features.append(\"has_capital_activity\")\n","\n","    # F4 — Hours category (ordinal binning)\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\", True):\n","        def hour_cat(h):\n","            if h < 35: return 0    # Part-time\n","            elif h <= 45: return 1 # Standard\n","            elif h <= 60: return 2 # Overtime\n","            else: return 3         # Extreme\n","        df_out[\"hours_category\"] = df_out[\"hours_per_week\"].apply(hour_cat)\n","        new_features.append(\"hours_category\")\n","\n","    # F5 — Education × Hours interaction\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_EDU_HOURS\", True):\n","        df_out[\"edu_hours_interaction\"] = df_out[\"educational_num\"] * df_out[\"hours_per_week\"]\n","        new_features.append(\"edu_hours_interaction\")\n","\n","    # F6 — Marital binary (is_married)\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\", True):\n","        if \"marital_status\" in df_out.columns:\n","            married_vals = {\"Married-civ-spouse\", \"Married-AF-spouse\"}\n","            df_out[\"is_married\"] = df_out[\"marital_status\"].isin(married_vals).astype(int)\n","        else:\n","            # Already label-encoded — skip gracefully\n","            df_out[\"is_married\"] = 0\n","        new_features.append(\"is_married\")\n","\n","    # F7 — High education flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\", True):\n","        df_out[\"is_high_edu\"] = (df_out[\"educational_num\"] >= 13).astype(int)\n","        new_features.append(\"is_high_edu\")\n","\n","    return df_out, new_features\n","\n","# Demonstrate the block\n","df_demo, new_feats = add_feature_block(df_modeling) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","print(f\"\\n  add_feature_block generated {len(new_feats)} features: {new_feats}\")\n","print(f\"  DataFrame shape before: {df_modeling.shape}  →  after: {df_demo.shape}\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# STRATIFIED K-FOLD EVALUATION + EXPERIMENT LOG + REGISTRY\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"STRATIFIED K-FOLD EVALUATION — EXPERIMENT LOG & REGISTRY\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","EXPERIMENT_LOG = []\n","FEATURE_REGISTRY = {}\n","\n","def run_experiment(exp_name, toggles, df_raw_in, baseline_results, n_splits=5):\n","    \"\"\"Run one experiment with given feature toggles; log results.\"\"\"\n","    t0 = time.time()\n","\n","    # Build features\n","    df_exp, new_feats = add_feature_block(df_raw_in, toggles)\n","\n","    # Fill missing, encode cats\n","    df_exp2 = prepare_baseline(df_exp)\n","\n","    active_features = [c for c in feat_cols if c in df_exp2.columns] + \\\n","                      [f for f in new_feats if f in df_exp2.columns]\n","    # Deduplicate\n","    active_features = list(dict.fromkeys(active_features))\n","\n","    X = df_exp2[active_features].fillna(0).values\n","    y_exp = df_exp2[SCHEMA[\"target\"]].values # Changed \"target\" to SCHEMA[\"target\"]\n","\n","    skf_ = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n","    model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","\n","    auc_scores = cross_val_score(model, X, y_exp, cv=skf_, scoring=\"roc_auc\")\n","    f1_scores  = cross_val_score(model, X, y_exp, cv=skf_, scoring=\"f1\")\n","\n","    delta_auc = auc_scores.mean() - baseline_results[\"auc_mean\"]\n","    delta_f1  = f1_scores.mean()  - baseline_results[\"f1_mean\"]\n","\n","    result = {\n","        \"experiment\": exp_name,\n","        \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n","        \"toggles\": {k: v for k, v in toggles.items() if v},\n","        \"n_features\": len(active_features),\n","        \"new_features\": new_feats,\n","        \"auc_mean\": round(auc_scores.mean(), 5),\n","        \"auc_std\":  round(auc_scores.std(), 5),\n","        \"f1_mean\":  round(f1_scores.mean(), 5),\n","        \"f1_std\":   round(f1_scores.std(), 5),\n","        \"delta_auc\": round(delta_auc, 5),\n","        \"delta_f1\":  round(delta_f1, 5),\n","        \"runtime_s\": round(time.time() - t0, 2),\n","        \"auc_cv\": [round(x, 5) for x in auc_scores.tolist()]\n","    }\n","    EXPERIMENT_LOG.append(result)\n","\n","    # Register each new feature\n","    for feat in new_feats:\n","        if feat not in FEATURE_REGISTRY:\n","            FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat] = {\n","                \"first_seen\": exp_name,\n","                \"delta_auc_history\": [],\n","                \"stable\": None\n","            }\n","        FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat][\"delta_auc_history\"].append(delta_auc)\n","\n","    return result\n","\n","print(\"\\n  Running experiments...\")\n","\n","# Experiment 1: All features ON\n","r1 = run_experiment(\"EXP01_ALL_FEATURES\", {\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": True,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": True\n","}, df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Experiment 2: Capital features only\n","r2 = run_experiment(\"EXP02_CAPITAL_ONLY\", {\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": False, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": False, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": False,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": False, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": False\n","}, df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Experiment 3: Interaction + Marital\n","r3 = run_experiment(\"EXP03_INTERACTION_MARITAL\", {\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": False, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": False, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": False,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": False, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": True,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": True\n","}, df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Experiment 4: No high-edu flag (ablation)\n","r4 = run_experiment(\"EXP04_NO_HIGH_EDU\", {\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": True,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": False\n","}, df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Experiment 5: Bins + Hours only\n","r5 = run_experiment(\"EXP05_BINS_HOURS\", {\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": False, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": False,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": False,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": False, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": False\n","}, df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS) # Changed df to df_modeling\n","\n","# Print experiment log\n","print(f\"\\n  {'Experiment':<35} {'AUC':>8} {'±':>6} {'ΔAUC':>8} {'F1':>7} {'ΔF1':>8} {'#Feat':>6}\")\n","print(\"  \" + \"-\"*82)\n","print(f\"  {'BASELINE':<35} {BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:.4f} {BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_std']:.4f} {'—':>8} {BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_mean']:.4f} {'—':>8} {BASELINE_RESULTS['n_features']:>6}\")\n","for r in EXPERIMENT_LOG:\n","    sign = \"+\" if r[\"delta_auc\"] >= 0 else \"\"\n","    sf   = \"+\" if r[\"delta_f1\"] >= 0 else \"\"\n","    print(f\"  {r['experiment']:<35} {r['auc_mean']:.4f} {r['auc_std']:.4f} {sign+str(r['delta_auc']):>8} {r['f1_mean']:.4f} {sf+str(r['delta_f1']):>8} {r['n_features']:>6}\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PRUNING: STABILITY + EFFECT SIZE\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"FEATURE PRUNING — STABILITY & EFFECT SIZE\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# Get feature importances from best experiment (EXP01 all features)\n","df_best, new_feats_best = add_feature_block(df_modeling, { # Changed df to df_modeling\n","    \"USE_AGE_BINS\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True,\n","    \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True, \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": True,\n","    \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": True\n","})\n","df_best2 = prepare_baseline(df_best)\n","all_feats = [c for c in feat_cols if c in df_best2.columns] + \\\n","            [f for f in new_feats_best if f in df_best2.columns]\n","all_feats = list(dict.fromkeys(all_feats))\n","\n","X_best = df_best2[all_feats].fillna(0).values\n","y_best = df_best2[SCHEMA[\"target\"]].values # Changed \"target\" to SCHEMA[\"target\"]\n","\n","# Collect fold-level importances for stability analysis\n","skf_prune = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n","importance_matrix = []\n","for train_idx, val_idx in skf_prune.split(X_best, y_best):\n","    m = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","    m.fit(X_best[train_idx], y_best[train_idx])\n","    importance_matrix.append(m.feature_importances_)\n","\n","importance_matrix = np.array(importance_matrix)\n","imp_mean = importance_matrix.mean(axis=0)\n","imp_std  = importance_matrix.std(axis=0)\n","imp_cv   = imp_std / (imp_mean + 1e-9)  # coefficient of variation (instability)\n","\n","feat_stability = pd.DataFrame({\n","    \"feature\": all_feats,\n","    \"imp_mean\": imp_mean,\n","    \"imp_std\":  imp_std,\n","    \"imp_cv\":   imp_cv,\n","}).sort_values(\"imp_mean\", ascending=False).reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","# Pruning criteria\n","EFFECT_THRESHOLD   = 0.010   # mean importance < 1% → low effect\n","STABILITY_THRESHOLD = 0.75   # CV > 0.75 → unstable\n","\n","feat_stability[\"prune_low_effect\"]  = feat_stability[\"imp_mean\"] < EFFECT_THRESHOLD\n","feat_stability[\"prune_unstable\"]    = feat_stability[\"imp_cv\"]   > STABILITY_THRESHOLD\n","feat_stability[\"PRUNE\"]             = feat_stability[\"prune_low_effect\"] | feat_stability[\"prune_unstable\"]\n","feat_stability[\"source\"]            = feat_stability[\"feature\"].apply(\n","    lambda f: \"NEW\" if f in new_feats_best else \"BASE\"\n",")\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Pruning thresholds: effect_size < {EFFECT_THRESHOLD} OR instability CV > {STABILITY_THRESHOLD}\")\n","print(f\"\\n  {'Feature':<28} {'Src':<5} {'ImpMean':>9} {'ImpCV':>7} {'LowEffect':>10} {'Unstable':>9} {'PRUNE':>7}\")\n","print(\"  \" + \"-\"*78)\n","for _, row in feat_stability.iterrows():\n","    prune_flag = \"✗ YES\" if row[\"PRUNE\"] else \"✓ KEEP\"\n","    le = \"YES\" if row[\"prune_low_effect\"] else \"no\"\n","    un = \"YES\" if row[\"prune_unstable\"] else \"no\"\n","    print(f\"  {row['feature']:<28} {row['source']:<5} {row['imp_mean']:>9.5f} {row['imp_cv']:>7.3f} {le:>10} {un:>9} {prune_flag:>7}\")\n","\n","pruned  = feat_stability[feat_stability[\"PRUNE\"]][\"feature\"].tolist()\n","kept    = feat_stability[~feat_stability[\"PRUNE\"]][\"feature\"].tolist()\n","new_kept   = [f for f in kept if f in new_feats_best]\n","new_pruned = [f for f in pruned if f in new_feats_best]\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Features KEPT    ({len(kept)}): {kept}\")\n","print(f\"  Features PRUNED  ({len(pruned)}): {pruned}\")\n","print(f\"\\n  New features kept  : {new_kept}\")\n","print(f\"  New features pruned: {new_pruned}\")\n","\n","# Final model with pruned feature set\n","print(\"\\n  Re-evaluating with pruned feature set...\")\n","X_pruned = df_best2[kept].fillna(0).values\n","pruned_model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","pruned_auc = cross_val_score(pruned_model, X_pruned, y_best, cv=skf_prune, scoring=\"roc_auc\")\n","pruned_f1  = cross_val_score(pruned_model, X_pruned, y_best, cv=skf_prune, scoring=\"f1\")\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Pruned model AUC : {pruned_auc.mean():.4f} ± {pruned_auc.std():.4f}  (Δ vs baseline: {pruned_auc.mean()-BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:+.4f})\")\n","print(f\"  Pruned model F1  : {pruned_f1.mean():.4f} ± {pruned_f1.std():.4f}  (Δ vs baseline: {pruned_f1.mean()-BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_mean']:+.4f})\")\n","print(f\"  Feature count    : {len(kept)} (was {len(all_feats)} before pruning)\")\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# SAVE ARTIFACTS\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"SAVING ARTIFACTS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# Experiment log JSON\n","log_path = \"/content/experiment_log.json\"\n","with open(log_path, \"w\") as f:\n","    json.dump({\n","        \"baseline\": BASELINE_RESULTS,\n","        \"experiments\": EXPERIMENT_LOG,\n","        \"feature_registry\": FEATURE_REGISTRY\n","    }, f, indent=2)\n","print(f\"\\n  Experiment log  → {log_path}\")\n","\n","# Feature registry / stability CSV\n","reg_path = \"/content/feature_registry.csv\"\n","feat_stability.to_csv(reg_path, index=False)\n","print(f\"  Feature registry → {reg_path}\")\n","\n","# Summary report\n","summary_path = \"/content/pipeline_summary.md\"\n","best_exp = max(EXPERIMENT_LOG, key=lambda x: x[\"auc_mean\"])\n","\n","with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n","    f.write(\"# UCI Adult Income — Feature Engineering Pipeline Summary\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"**Run date:** {datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')}\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"## Dataset\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- Rows: {len(df_modeling):,}\\n\") # Changed df to df_modeling\n","    f.write(f\"- Target: income >50K (positive class = {df_modeling[SCHEMA['target']].mean():.1%})\\n\\n\") # Changed df to df_modeling\n","    f.write(\"## Baseline\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- AUC: `{BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:.4f} ± {BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_std']:.4f}`\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- F1:  `{BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_mean']:.4f} ± {BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_std']:.4f}`\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"## Feature Proposals (7 total, all pass leakage check)\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"| ID | Name | Type | Impact |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","    for p in FEATURE_PROPOSALS:\n","        f.write(f\"| {p['id']} | `{p['name']}` | {p['type']} | {p['expected_impact']} |\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"\\n## Experiment Results\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"| Experiment | AUC | ΔAUC | F1 | ΔF1 |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"| BASELINE | {BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:.4f} | — | {BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_mean']:.4f} | — |\\n\")\n","    for r in EXPERIMENT_LOG:\n","        f.write(f\"| {r['experiment']} | {r['auc_mean']:.4f} | {r['delta_auc']:+.4f} | {r['f1_mean']:.4f} | {r['delta_f1']:+.4f} |\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"\\n**Best experiment:** `{best_exp['experiment']}` — AUC `{best_exp['auc_mean']:.4f}`\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"## Pruning Results\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- Thresholds: importance < {EFFECT_THRESHOLD} OR CV > {STABILITY_THRESHOLD}\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- Features kept: {len(kept)}\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- Features pruned: {len(pruned)}\\n\")\n","    if pruned:\n","        f.write(f\"- Pruned: {', '.join(f'`{p}`' for p in pruned)}\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"\\n**Pruned model AUC:** `{pruned_auc.mean():.4f} ± {pruned_auc.std():.4f}` (Δ: `{pruned_auc.mean()-BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:+.4f}`)\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"**Pruned model F1:**  `{pruned_f1.mean():.4f} ± {pruned_f1.std():.4f}`\\n\")\n","\n","print(f\"  Pipeline summary → {summary_path}\")\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PIPELINE COMPLETE ✓\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 2 — TEMPLATE B: FEATURE ENGINEERING FOR RECALL / FALSE-NEGATIVE REDUCTION\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"TEMPLATE B — PHASE 2: FALSE-NEGATIVE REDUCTION FEATURES\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# ── B.1  New feature proposals targeting false negatives ──────────────────\n","TEMPLATE_B_PROPOSALS = [\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B1\",\n","        \"name\": \"high_capital_gain_flag\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binary Indicator\",\n","        \"description\": \"is_high_capital_gain = 1 if capital_gain > 5000. \"\n","                       \"Non-zero capital activity is a strong >50K signal often missed \"\n","                       \"when treated as continuous (most values are 0).\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Captures sparse but decisive signal; model misses these \"\n","                        \"because linear scaling dilutes extreme values.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — capital_gain is a census-time observation.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"HIGH recall uplift for >50K cases with investment income.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B2\",\n","        \"name\": \"exec_managerial_flag\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binary Indicator from Grouping\",\n","        \"description\": \"is_exec_mgr = 1 if occupation in {Exec-managerial, Prof-specialty}. \"\n","                       \"High-income occupations are consistently under-identified.\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Reduces FN for white-collar workers whose other features \"\n","                        \"(e.g., moderate hours) appear 'average'.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — occupation is an input feature.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — targets systematic under-prediction in professions.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_EXEC_MGR_FLAG\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B3\",\n","        \"name\": \"married_highEdu_interaction\",\n","        \"type\": \"Multiplicative Interaction\",\n","        \"description\": \"married_edu = is_married × educational_num. \"\n","                       \"Married high-educated individuals are the most under-predicted >50K group.\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Interaction creates a distinct high-income profile cluster not \"\n","                        \"separately captured by either feature alone.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — both components are pre-survey inputs.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"HIGH — the FN-heavy subgroup is precisely married + educated.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_MARRIED_EDU\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B4\",\n","        \"name\": \"age_edu_interaction\",\n","        \"type\": \"Multiplicative Interaction\",\n","        \"description\": \"age_edu = age × educational_num. Captures mid-career educated \"\n","                       \"workers whose salaries peak but aren't flagged.\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Reduces FN for prime-age (35–55) professionals; raw age + edu \"\n","                        \"alone underweight combined effect.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — both age and educational_num are survey-time inputs.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM-HIGH — targets career-peak false negatives.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_AGE_EDU\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B5\",\n","        \"name\": \"overtime_professional_flag\",\n","        \"type\": \"Composite Indicator\",\n","        \"description\": \"is_overtime_pro = 1 if hours_per_week > 45 AND \"\n","                       \"occupation in {Exec-managerial, Prof-specialty, Tech-support}. \"\n","                       \"Hard-working professionals are frequently missed.\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Synthesises hours and role to flag the 'overworked professional' \"\n","                        \"archetype that drives many >50K FNs.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — hours and occupation are independent survey responses.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"MEDIUM — niche but high-precision uplift for this subgroup.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_OVERTIME_PRO\"\n","    },\n","    {\n","        \"id\": \"B6\",\n","        \"name\": \"private_sector_flag\",\n","        \"type\": \"Binary Grouping\",\n","        \"description\": \"is_private = 1 if workclass == 'Private'. \"\n","                       \"Private-sector workers form the majority and are systematically \"\n","                       \"under-identified when >50K.\",\n","        \"fn_rationale\": \"Explicit indicator helps model attend to within-private variation \"\n","                        \"more carefully; baseline lumps all non-government workers.\",\n","        \"leakage_check\": \"PASS — workclass is a survey-time field.\",\n","        \"expected_impact\": \"LOW-MEDIUM — modest but consistent recall improvement.\",\n","        \"toggle\": \"USE_PRIVATE_FLAG\"\n","    },\n","]\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Total Template B proposals: {len(TEMPLATE_B_PROPOSALS)}\")\n","print(f\"\\n  {'ID':<4} {'Name':<32} {'Type':<28} {'Leakage':<8}\")\n","print(\"  \" + \"-\"*78)\n","for p in TEMPLATE_B_PROPOSALS:\n","    status = \"✓ PASS\" if \"PASS\" in p[\"leakage_check\"] else \"✗ FAIL\"\n","    print(f\"  {p['id']:<4} {p['name']:<32} {p['type']:<28} {status}\")\n","\n","# ── B.2  Implementation: add_fn_features ─────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"add_fn_features — IMPLEMENTATION WITH TOGGLES\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","def add_fn_features(df_in, toggles=None):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Add false-negative–reduction features to the dataframe.\n","\n","    Parameters\n","    ----------\n","    df_in   : pd.DataFrame  — preprocessed dataframe (fnlwgt excluded).\n","    toggles : dict          — feature on/off switches; defaults: all ON.\n","\n","    Returns\n","    -------\n","    df_out      : pd.DataFrame  — extended dataframe\n","    new_features: list[str]     — names of added columns\n","    \"\"\"\n","    DEFAULT_TOGGLES = {\n","        \"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True,\n","        \"USE_EXEC_MGR_FLAG\":     True,\n","        \"USE_MARRIED_EDU\":       True,\n","        \"USE_AGE_EDU\":           True,\n","        \"USE_OVERTIME_PRO\":      True,\n","        \"USE_PRIVATE_FLAG\":      True,\n","    }\n","    if toggles is None:\n","        toggles = DEFAULT_TOGGLES\n","    else:\n","        toggles = {**DEFAULT_TOGGLES, **toggles}\n","\n","    df_out = df_in.copy()\n","    new_features = []\n","\n","    # B1 — High capital gain binary flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\", True):\n","        df_out[\"high_capital_gain_flag\"] = (\n","            pd.to_numeric(df_out[\"capital_gain\"], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0) > 5000\n","        ).astype(int)\n","        new_features.append(\"high_capital_gain_flag\")\n","\n","    # B2 — Executive / managerial role flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_EXEC_MGR_FLAG\", True):\n","        if \"occupation\" in df_out.columns:\n","            exec_occ = {\"Exec-managerial\", \"Prof-specialty\"}\n","            df_out[\"exec_managerial_flag\"] = df_out[\"occupation\"].isin(exec_occ).astype(int)\n","        else:\n","            df_out[\"exec_managerial_flag\"] = 0\n","        new_features.append(\"exec_managerial_flag\")\n","\n","    # B3 — Married × Education interaction\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_MARRIED_EDU\", True):\n","        married_vals = {\"Married-civ-spouse\", \"Married-AF-spouse\"}\n","        if \"marital_status\" in df_out.columns:\n","            is_married = df_out[\"marital_status\"].isin(married_vals).astype(int)\n","        else:\n","            is_married = df_out.get(\"is_married\", pd.Series(0, index=df_out.index))\n","        edu_num = pd.to_numeric(df_out.get(\"educational_num\", df_out.get(\"educational_num\", 0)),\n","                                errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0)\n","        df_out[\"married_highEdu_interaction\"] = is_married * edu_num\n","        new_features.append(\"married_highEdu_interaction\")\n","\n","    # B4 — Age × Education interaction\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_AGE_EDU\", True):\n","        age = pd.to_numeric(df_out[\"age\"], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(df_out[\"age\"].median())\n","        edu_num = pd.to_numeric(df_out.get(\"educational_num\", df_out.get(\"educational_num\", 0)),\n","                                errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0)\n","        df_out[\"age_edu_interaction\"] = age * edu_num\n","        new_features.append(\"age_edu_interaction\")\n","\n","    # B5 — Overtime professional composite flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_OVERTIME_PRO\", True):\n","        hrs = pd.to_numeric(df_out[\"hours_per_week\"], errors=\"coerce\").fillna(0)\n","        if \"occupation\" in df_out.columns:\n","            pro_occ = {\"Exec-managerial\", \"Prof-specialty\", \"Tech-support\"}\n","            is_pro = df_out[\"occupation\"].isin(pro_occ).astype(int)\n","        else:\n","            is_pro = pd.Series(0, index=df_out.index)\n","        df_out[\"overtime_professional_flag\"] = ((hrs > 45) & (is_pro == 1)).astype(int)\n","        new_features.append(\"overtime_professional_flag\")\n","\n","    # B6 — Private sector flag\n","    if toggles.get(\"USE_PRIVATE_FLAG\", True):\n","        if \"workclass\" in df_out.columns:\n","            df_out[\"private_sector_flag\"] = (df_out[\"workclass\"] == \"Private\").astype(int)\n","        else:\n","            df_out[\"private_sector_flag\"] = 0\n","        new_features.append(\"private_sector_flag\")\n","\n","    return df_out, new_features\n","\n","\n","# Demonstrate\n","df_demo_b, new_feats_b = add_fn_features(df_modeling)\n","print(f\"\\n  add_fn_features generated {len(new_feats_b)} features: {new_feats_b}\")\n","print(f\"  DataFrame shape before: {df_modeling.shape}  →  after: {df_demo_b.shape}\")\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 2 — ABLATION EXPERIMENTS: RECALL-ORIENTED EVALUATION\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PHASE 2 — ABLATION EXPERIMENTS (RECALL / F1 FOCUS)\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# Combined feature adder (Template A + Template B)\n","def add_all_features(df_in, toggles_a=None, toggles_b=None):\n","    df1, feats_a = add_feature_block(df_in, toggles_a)\n","    df2, feats_b = add_fn_features(df1, toggles_b)\n","    return df2, feats_a + feats_b\n","\n","\n","def run_recall_experiment(exp_name, toggles_a, toggles_b, df_raw_in,\n","                          baseline_results, n_splits=5):\n","    \"\"\"\n","    Evaluate with recall as primary metric alongside AUC and F1.\n","    Stores results in EXPERIMENT_LOG and FEATURE_REGISTRY.\n","    \"\"\"\n","    t0 = time.time()\n","    df_exp, new_feats = add_all_features(df_raw_in, toggles_a, toggles_b)\n","    df_exp2 = prepare_baseline(df_exp)\n","\n","    base_feats = [c for c in feat_cols if c in df_exp2.columns]\n","    eng_feats  = [f for f in new_feats if f in df_exp2.columns]\n","    active_features = list(dict.fromkeys(base_feats + eng_feats))\n","\n","    X = df_exp2[active_features].fillna(0).values\n","    y_exp = df_exp2[SCHEMA[\"target\"]].values\n","\n","    skf_ = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=n_splits, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n","    model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","\n","    scoring = {\"auc\": \"roc_auc\", \"f1\": \"f1\", \"recall\": \"recall\", \"precision\": \"precision\"}\n","    cv_res = cross_validate(model, X, y_exp, cv=skf_, scoring=scoring)\n","\n","    auc_scores = cv_res[\"test_auc\"]\n","    f1_scores  = cv_res[\"test_f1\"]\n","    rec_scores = cv_res[\"test_recall\"]\n","    pre_scores = cv_res[\"test_precision\"]\n","\n","    delta_auc    = auc_scores.mean() - baseline_results[\"auc_mean\"]\n","    delta_f1     = f1_scores.mean()  - baseline_results[\"f1_mean\"]\n","    delta_recall = rec_scores.mean() - baseline_results.get(\"recall_mean\", rec_scores.mean())\n","\n","    result = {\n","        \"experiment\": exp_name,\n","        \"timestamp\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n","        \"phase\": \"B\",\n","        \"n_features\": len(active_features),\n","        \"new_features\": new_feats,\n","        \"auc_mean\":       round(auc_scores.mean().item(), 5),\n","        \"auc_std\":        round(auc_scores.std().item(),  5),\n","        \"f1_mean\":        round(f1_scores.mean().item(),  5),\n","        \"f1_std\":         round(f1_scores.std().item(),   5),\n","        \"recall_mean\":    round(rec_scores.mean().item(), 5),\n","        \"recall_std\":     round(rec_scores.std().item(),  5),\n","        \"precision_mean\": round(pre_scores.mean().item(), 5),\n","        \"delta_auc\":      round(delta_auc.item(),    5),\n","        \"delta_f1\":       round(delta_f1.item(),     5),\n","        \"delta_recall\":   round(delta_recall.item(), 5),\n","        \"runtime_s\":      round(time.time() - t0, 2),\n","        \"recall_cv\": [round(x, 5) for x in rec_scores.tolist()],\n","        \"auc_cv\":    [round(x, 5) for x in auc_scores.tolist()],\n","    }\n","    EXPERIMENT_LOG.append(result)\n","\n","    # Update feature registry\n","    for feat in new_feats:\n","        if feat not in FEATURE_REGISTRY:\n","            FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat] = {\n","                \"first_seen\": exp_name,\n","                \"delta_auc_history\":    [],\n","                \"delta_recall_history\": [],\n","                \"stable\": None,\n","                \"rejected\": False,\n","                \"rejection_reason\": None\n","            }\n","        if \"delta_recall_history\" not in FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat]:\n","          FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat][\"delta_recall_history\"] = []\n","        FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat][\"delta_auc_history\"].append(float(delta_auc))\n","        FEATURE_REGISTRY[feat][\"delta_recall_history\"].append(float(delta_recall))\n","\n","    return result\n","\n","\n","# ── ALL features on (Template A + Template B) ────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n  Running Template B ablation experiments...\")\n","\n","ALL_A = {\"USE_AGE_BINS\": True, \"USE_CAPITAL_NET\": True, \"USE_HOURS_CATEGORY\": True,\n","         \"USE_EDU_HOURS\": True, \"USE_MARITAL_BINARY\": True, \"USE_HIGH_EDU_FLAG\": True}\n","ALL_B = {\"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True, \"USE_EXEC_MGR_FLAG\": True,\n","         \"USE_MARRIED_EDU\": True, \"USE_AGE_EDU\": True,\n","         \"USE_OVERTIME_PRO\": True, \"USE_PRIVATE_FLAG\": True}\n","OFF_A = {k: False for k in ALL_A}\n","OFF_B = {k: False for k in ALL_B}\n","\n","# Fully scalable experiment registry\n","SCENARIOS = [\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP01_ALL_AB\", \"a\": ALL_A, \"b\": ALL_B},\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP02_FN_ONLY\", \"a\": OFF_A, \"b\": ALL_B},\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP03_NO_CAPITAL_FLAG\", \"a\": ALL_A, \"b\": {**ALL_B, \"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\": False}},\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP04_NO_MARRIED_EDU\", \"a\": ALL_A, \"b\": {**ALL_B, \"USE_MARRIED_EDU\": False}},\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP05_INTERACTIONS_ONLY\", \"a\": ALL_A, \"b\": {**OFF_B, \"USE_MARRIED_EDU\": True, \"USE_AGE_EDU\": True}},\n","    {\"id\": \"B_EXP06_INDICATORS_ONLY\", \"a\": ALL_A, \"b\": {**OFF_B, \"USE_HIGH_CAPITAL_FLAG\": True, \"USE_EXEC_MGR_FLAG\": True, \"USE_OVERTIME_PRO\": True, \"USE_PRIVATE_FLAG\": True}},\n","]\n","\n","phase_b_results = [\n","    run_recall_experiment(s[\"id\"], s[\"a\"], s[\"b\"], df_modeling, BASELINE_RESULTS)\n","    for s in SCENARIOS\n","]\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 2 — ROBUSTNESS: FOLD VARIANCE & HOLDOUT CONSISTENCY\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PHASE 2 — ROBUSTNESS VALIDATION\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","VARIANCE_THRESHOLD  = 0.025   # std across folds > this → unstable\n","HOLDOUT_DROP_LIMIT  = 0.010   # val→test AUC drop > this → inconsistent\n","\n","print(f\"\\n  Thresholds:  fold_std > {VARIANCE_THRESHOLD} → unstable | \"\n","      f\"holdout_drop > {HOLDOUT_DROP_LIMIT} → inconsistent\")\n","print(f\"\\n  {'Experiment':<38} {'RecallStd':>10} {'AUCStd':>8} {'Stable?':>8}\")\n","print(\"  \" + \"-\"*68)\n","\n","for r in phase_b_results:\n","    rec_std = r[\"recall_std\"]\n","    auc_std = r[\"auc_std\"]\n","    stable  = \"✓ YES\" if (rec_std < VARIANCE_THRESHOLD and auc_std < VARIANCE_THRESHOLD) else \"✗ NO\"\n","    print(f\"  {r['experiment']:<38} {rec_std:>10.5f} {auc_std:>8.5f} {stable:>8}\")\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 2 — FEATURE REGISTRY UPDATE & REJECTION LOG\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PHASE 2 — FEATURE REGISTRY UPDATE & REJECTION LOG\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","REJECTION_LOG = []\n","\n","# Evaluate registry stability from ablation history\n","for feat, meta in FEATURE_REGISTRY.items():\n","    hist = meta.get(\"delta_recall_history\", [])\n","    auc_hist = meta.get(\"delta_auc_history\", [])\n","    if len(hist) >= 2:\n","        recall_variance = float(np.std(hist))\n","        auc_variance    = float(np.std(auc_hist))\n","        avg_delta_recall = float(np.mean(hist))\n","\n","        # Rejection criteria\n","        reject = False\n","        reason = None\n","        if recall_variance > VARIANCE_THRESHOLD:\n","            reject = True\n","            reason = f\"Instability: recall_delta_std={recall_variance:.4f} > {VARIANCE_THRESHOLD}\"\n","        elif avg_delta_recall < -0.005:\n","            reject = True\n","            reason = f\"Negative recall impact: mean_delta_recall={avg_delta_recall:.4f}\"\n","\n","        meta[\"stable\"]           = not reject\n","        meta[\"rejected\"]         = reject\n","        meta[\"rejection_reason\"] = reason\n","        if reject:\n","            REJECTION_LOG.append({\"feature\": feat, \"reason\": reason})\n","            print(f\"  ✗ REJECTED — {feat}: {reason}\")\n","        else:\n","            print(f\"  ✓ RETAINED  — {feat}: avg_δrecall={avg_delta_recall:+.4f}, std={recall_variance:.4f}\")\n","\n","if REJECTION_LOG:\n","    print(f\"\\n  {len(REJECTION_LOG)} feature(s) rejected and flagged in registry.\")\n","else:\n","    print(\"\\n  No features rejected — all pass stability and recall criteria.\")\n","\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"TEMPLATE B PIPELINE COMPLETE ✓\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 3 — FAIRNESS DIAGNOSTICS\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PHASE 3 — FAIRNESS DIAGNOSTICS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# Build best feature set from Phase B (all A + all B)\n","df_fair, all_feats_fair = add_all_features(df_modeling, ALL_A, ALL_B)\n","df_fair2 = prepare_baseline(df_fair)\n","\n","# Preserve sensitive cols before they get label-encoded\n","sensitive_cols_raw = [\"sex\", \"race\", \"gender\", \"marital_status\"]\n","available_sensitive = [c for c in sensitive_cols_raw if c in df_modeling.columns] # Changed df_modeling to use consistent variable\n","\n","# Keep original categorical labels for subgroup analysis\n","df_fair_meta = df_modeling[available_sensitive + [SCHEMA[\"target\"]]].copy() # Changed df_modeling to use consistent variable\n","\n","base_feats   = [c for c in feat_cols if c in df_fair2.columns]\n","eng_feats_ok = [f for f in all_feats_fair if f in df_fair2.columns]\n","final_feats  = list(dict.fromkeys(base_feats + eng_feats_ok))\n","\n","X_fair = df_fair2[final_feats].fillna(0).values\n","y_fair = df_fair2[SCHEMA[\"target\"]].values\n","\n","\n","\n","# Train model on full data for fairness evaluation\n","fair_model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","from sklearn.model_selection import cross_val_predict\n","\n","\n","y_prob_cv = cross_val_predict(fair_model, X_fair, y_fair, cv=5, method=\"predict_proba\")[:, 1]\n","fair_model.fit(X_fair, y_fair)\n","y_pred_fair = fair_model.predict(X_fair)\n","y_prob_fair = fair_model.predict_proba(X_fair)[:, 1]\n","\n","# 3. OVERALL Confusion Matrix\n","from sklearn.metrics import confusion_matrix, ConfusionMatrixDisplay\n","import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n","\n","print(\"--- OVERALL CONFUSION MATRIX ---\")\n","cm_overall = confusion_matrix(y_fair, y_pred_fair)\n","print(cm_overall)\n","\n","\n"," # Re-align indices\n","df_fair_meta = df_fair_meta.loc[df_fair2.index].reset_index(drop=True)\n","y_fair_aligned    = pd.Series(y_fair)\n","y_pred_aligned    = pd.Series(y_pred_fair)\n","y_prob_aligned    = pd.Series(y_prob_fair)\n","\n","\n","def subgroup_metrics(df_meta, y_true, y_pred, y_prob, group_col):\n","    \"\"\"Compute TPR, FPR, Precision, Recall, F1, AUC by subgroup.\"\"\"\n","    records = []\n","    for g in df_meta[group_col].dropna().unique():\n","        idx = (df_meta[group_col] == g).values\n","        if idx.sum() < 30:\n","            continue\n","        yt  = y_true[idx]\n","        yp  = y_pred[idx]\n","        ypr = y_prob[idx]\n","\n","        tn, fp, fn, tp = confusion_matrix(yt, yp, labels=[0, 1]).ravel()\n","        tpr  = tp / (tp + fn + 1e-9)\n","        fpr  = fp / (fp + tn + 1e-9)\n","        prec = tp / (tp + fp + 1e-9)\n","        rec  = tpr\n","        f1   = 2 * prec * rec / (prec + rec + 1e-9)\n","        auc  = roc_auc_score(yt, ypr) if len(set(yt)) > 1 else float(\"nan\")\n","        fn_rate = fn / (fn + tp + 1e-9)\n","\n","        records.append({\n","            \"group\": g, \"n\": int(idx.sum()),\n","            \"TPR\":  round(tpr,  4), \"FPR\": round(fpr, 4),\n","            \"Precision\": round(prec, 4), \"Recall\": round(rec, 4),\n","            \"F1\":  round(f1,   4), \"AUC\": round(auc, 4),\n","            \"FN_rate\": round(fn_rate, 4),\n","            \"TP\": int(tp), \"FP\": int(fp), \"FN\": int(fn), \"TN\": int(tn)\n","        })\n","    return pd.DataFrame(records).sort_values(\"AUC\", ascending=False)\n","\n","\n","FAIRNESS_RESULTS = {}\n","for col in available_sensitive:\n","    print(f\"\\n  === Subgroup metrics by {col.upper()} ===\")\n","    fm = subgroup_metrics(df_fair_meta, y_fair_aligned, y_pred_aligned, y_prob_aligned, col)\n","    FAIRNESS_RESULTS[col] = fm.to_dict(\"records\")\n","    print(fm[[\"group\", \"n\", \"AUC\", \"TPR\", \"FPR\", \"Precision\", \"Recall\", \"F1\", \"FN_rate\"]].to_string(index=False))\n","\n","    if len(fm) >= 2:\n","        max_auc, min_auc = fm[\"AUC\"].max(), fm[\"AUC\"].min()\n","        max_tpr, min_tpr = fm[\"TPR\"].max(), fm[\"TPR\"].min()\n","        print(f\"\\n  AUC gap  : {max_auc:.4f} – {min_auc:.4f} = {max_auc-min_auc:.4f}\")\n","        print(f\"  TPR gap  : {max_tpr:.4f} – {min_tpr:.4f} = {max_tpr-min_tpr:.4f}\")\n","        if (max_auc - min_auc) > 0.05:\n","            print(f\"  ⚠  FAIRNESS ALERT: AUC disparity > 5pp across {col} groups.\")\n","        if (max_tpr - min_tpr) > 0.10:\n","            print(f\"  ⚠  FAIRNESS ALERT: TPR disparity > 10pp across {col} groups.\")\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 3 — FINAL INTEGRATED EVALUATION (60/20/20)(Fairness migitation and Train + Evaluation on holdout test set )\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"FINAL INTEGRATED MODEL: CALIBRATION & HOLDOUT EVALUATION\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split as tts\n","\n","# 1. Unified 60/20/20 Split\n","indices = np.arange(len(X_fair))\n","# Create 80/20 Split\n","train_val_idx, holdout_idx = tts(indices, test_size=0.20, stratify=y_fair, random_state=42)\n","# Split 80 into 60/20\n","train_idx, val_idx = tts(train_val_idx, test_size=0.25, stratify=y_fair[train_val_idx], random_state=42)\n","\n","# Slice Data\n","X_train, y_train = X_fair[train_idx], y_fair[train_idx]\n","X_val,   y_val   = X_fair[val_idx],   y_fair[val_idx]\n","X_hold,  y_hold  = X_fair[holdout_idx], y_fair[holdout_idx]\n","\n","# Slice Metadata (crucial for per-group thresholds)\n","meta_val  = df_fair_meta.iloc[val_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n","meta_hold = df_fair_meta.iloc[holdout_idx].reset_index(drop=True)\n","\n","# 2. Train Model\n","final_model = GradientBoostingClassifier(n_estimators=100, random_state=42)\n","final_model.fit(X_train, y_train)\n","\n","# 3. Calibrate on Validation Set (The 20% 'Val')\n","y_prob_val = final_model.predict_proba(X_val)[:, 1]\n","TARGET_RECALL = 0.70\n","group_thresholds = {}\n","mitigation_col = available_sensitive[0]\n","for g in meta_val[mitigation_col].unique():\n","    idx = (meta_val[mitigation_col] == g).values\n","    if idx.sum() < 10: continue\n","    fpr, tpr, thresholds = roc_curve(y_val[idx], y_prob_val[idx])\n","    valid_idx = np.where(tpr >= TARGET_RECALL)[0]\n","    group_thresholds[g] = float(thresholds[valid_idx[0]]) if len(valid_idx) > 0 else 0.5\n","\n","# 4. Evaluate on Holdout Set (The 20% 'Holdout')\n","y_prob_hold = final_model.predict_proba(X_hold)[:, 1]\n","y_pred_final = np.zeros_like(y_prob_hold)\n","\n","for g, thresh in group_thresholds.items():\n","    mask = (meta_hold[mitigation_col] == g).values\n","    y_pred_final[mask] = (y_prob_hold[mask] >= thresh).astype(int)\n","\n","# 5. Final Reporting\n","print(f\"Holdout Size: {len(y_hold)} | Features: {X_train.shape[1]}\")\n","print(\"\\nClassification Report (Mitigated Holdout):\")\n","print(classification_report(y_hold, y_pred_final, target_names=[\"<=50K\", \">50K\"]))\n","\n","# Store in FINAL_RESULTS for your log file\n","auc_fin = roc_auc_score(y_hold, y_prob_hold)\n","p, r, f1, _ = precision_recall_fscore_support(y_hold, y_pred_final, average=\"binary\")\n","FINAL_RESULTS = {\"AUC\": auc_fin, \"F1\": f1, \"Recall\": r, \"Precision\": p, \"n_features\": X_train.shape[1]}\n","\n","# Calculates the differences with this mitigated model and the earlier baseline\n","base_auc = BASELINE_RESULTS.get(\"auc_mean\", 0)\n","base_f1  = BASELINE_RESULTS.get(\"f1_mean\", 0)\n","\n","# Inject the new keys\n","FINAL_RESULTS[\"delta_auc_vs_baseline\"] = FINAL_RESULTS[\"AUC\"] - base_auc\n","FINAL_RESULTS[\"delta_f1_vs_baseline\"]  = FINAL_RESULTS[\"F1\"]  - base_f1\n","\n","# Print the sample sizes used\n","print(f\" DATA SPLIT SUMMARY (60/20/20)\")\n","print(f\"-----------------------------------\")\n","print(f\"Total Samples Trained On : {len(y_train)}\")\n","print(f\"Total Samples Validated  : {len(y_val)}\")\n","print(f\"Total Samples Tested     : {len(y_hold)}\")\n","print(f\"Number of Features       : {FINAL_RESULTS['n_features']}\")\n","\n","# Print the final performance metrics\n","print(f\"\\n FINAL TEST RESULTS (MITIGATED)\")\n","print(f\"-----------------------------------\")\n","print(f\"AUC Score    : {FINAL_RESULTS['AUC']:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"F1-Score     : {FINAL_RESULTS['F1']:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Recall       : {FINAL_RESULTS['Recall']:.4f}\")\n","print(f\"Precision    : {FINAL_RESULTS['Precision']:.4f}\")\n","\n","# Compare against baseline (the Deltas)\n","print(f\"\\n FAIRNESS IMPACT\")\n","print(f\"-----------------------------------\")\n","print(f\"AUC Delta vs Baseline : {FINAL_RESULTS['delta_auc_vs_baseline']:+.4f}\")\n","print(f\"F1 Delta vs Baseline  : {FINAL_RESULTS['delta_f1_vs_baseline']:+.4f}\")\n","\n","MITIGATION_RESULTS = {\n","    \"group_thresholds\": group_thresholds,\n","    \"target_recall\": TARGET_RECALL,\n","    \"mitigation_column\": mitigation_col\n","}\n","\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","# PHASE 4 — SAVE ALL ARTIFACTS\n","# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\n","print(\"PHASE 4 — SAVING ALL ARTIFACTS\")\n","print(\"=\" * 70)\n","\n","# 1. Full experiment log JSON\n","log_path = \"/content/experiment_log_full.json\"\n","with open(log_path, \"w\") as f:\n","    json.dump({\n","        \"run_date\": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n","        \"baseline\": BASELINE_RESULTS,\n","        \"experiments\": EXPERIMENT_LOG,\n","        \"feature_registry\": FEATURE_REGISTRY,\n","        \"rejection_log\": REJECTION_LOG,\n","        \"fairness_results\": FAIRNESS_RESULTS,\n","        \"mitigation_results\": MITIGATION_RESULTS,\n","        \"final_results\": FINAL_RESULTS,\n","    }, f, indent=2)\n","print(f\"  Experiment log (full)   → {log_path}\")\n","\n","# 2. Feature registry CSV\n","registry_rows = []\n","for feat, meta in FEATURE_REGISTRY.items():\n","    registry_rows.append({\n","        \"feature\":          feat,\n","        \"first_seen\":       meta.get(\"first_seen\", \"\"),\n","        \"stable\":           meta.get(\"stable\", \"\"),\n","        \"rejected\":         meta.get(\"rejected\", False),\n","        \"rejection_reason\": meta.get(\"rejection_reason\", \"\"),\n","        \"avg_delta_auc\":    round(np.mean(meta.get(\"delta_auc_history\", [0])), 5),\n","        \"avg_delta_recall\": round(np.mean(meta.get(\"delta_recall_history\", [0])), 5),\n","    })\n","reg_df = pd.DataFrame(registry_rows)\n","reg_path = \"/content/feature_registry_full.csv\"\n","reg_df.to_csv(reg_path, index=False)\n","print(f\"  Feature registry (full) → {reg_path}\")\n","\n","# 3. Fairness report CSV\n","fairness_rows = []\n","for group_col, records in FAIRNESS_RESULTS.items():\n","    for rec in records:\n","        fairness_rows.append({\"sensitive_attr\": group_col, **rec})\n","fairness_df = pd.DataFrame(fairness_rows)\n","fairness_path = \"/content/fairness_report.csv\"\n","fairness_df.to_csv(fairness_path, index=False)\n","print(f\"  Fairness report         → {fairness_path}\")\n","\n","\n","# 4. Markdown performance summary\n","snapshot_info = {\n","    \"run_date\": datetime.now().strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M')\n","}\n","summary_path = \"/content/pipeline_summary_full.md\"\n","best_b = max([r for r in EXPERIMENT_LOG if r.get(\"phase\") == \"B\"],\n","             key=lambda x: x[\"auc_mean\"], default=None)\n","\n","audit_path = \"/content/fairness_audit_summary.md\"\n","with open(summary_path, \"w\") as f:\n","    f.write(\"# UCI Adult Income — FeatureBot Complete Pipeline Summary\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"**Run date:** {snapshot_info['run_date']}\\n\\n\")\n","\n","    f.write(\"## Phase 1 — Baseline\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- AUC: `{BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_mean']:.4f} ± {BASELINE_RESULTS['auc_std']:.4f}`\\n\")\n","    f.write(f\"- F1:  `{BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_mean']:.4f} ± {BASELINE_RESULTS['f1_std']:.4f}`\\n\\n\")\n","\n","    f.write(\"## Phase 2 — Template B (FN Reduction) Feature Proposals\\n\\n\")\n","    f.write(\"| ID | Name | FN Rationale | Leakage |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","    for p in TEMPLATE_B_PROPOSALS:\n","        f.write(f\"| {p['id']} | `{p['name']}` | {p['fn_rationale']} | PASS |\\n\")\n","\n","\n","\n","    if best_b:\n","        f.write(f\"\\n**Best Phase B experiment:** `{best_b['experiment']}` — \"\n","                f\"AUC `{best_b['auc_mean']:.4f}`, Recall `{best_b['recall_mean']:.4f}`\\n\\n\")\n","\n","    if REJECTION_LOG:\n","        f.write(\"## Rejected Features\\n\\n\")\n","        f.write(\"| Feature | Reason |\\n|---|---|\\n\")\n","        for rej in REJECTION_LOG:\n","            f.write(f\"| `{rej['feature']}` | {rej['reason']} |\\n\")\n","        f.write(\"\\n\")\n","\n","    f.write(\"## Phase 3 — Fairness Diagnostics\\n\\n\")\n","    for attr, records in FAIRNESS_RESULTS.items():\n","        f.write(f\"### By {attr}\\n\\n\")\n","        f.write(\"| Group | n | AUC | TPR | FPR | FN_rate |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","        for rec in records:\n","            f.write(f\"| {rec['group']} | {rec['n']} | {rec['AUC']:.4f} | \"\n","                    f\"{rec['TPR']:.4f} | {rec['FPR']:.4f} | {rec['FN_rate']:.4f} |\\n\")\n","        f.write(\"\\n\")\n","\n","    # --- 5. DOCUMENTATION AND FILE EXPORT ---\n","    # Calculate baseline delta (ensure BASELINE_RESULTS exists from Phase 1)\n","    baseline_auc = BASELINE_RESULTS.get(\"auc_mean\", 0)\n","    baseline_f1 = BASELINE_RESULTS.get(\"f1_mean\", 0)\n","\n","    # --- PHASE 4: SAVE THE DATA ---\n","    with open(audit_path, \"a\") as f_audit:\n","      f.write(\"\\n\" + \"─\" * 80 + \"\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"## PHASE 4 — FINAL CONSOLIDATED EVALUATION (60/20/20)\\n\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| Metric | Value | Δ vs Baseline |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| AUC | `{FINAL_RESULTS['AUC']:.4f}` | `{FINAL_RESULTS['delta_auc_vs_baseline']:+.4f}` |\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| F1 | `{FINAL_RESULTS['F1']:.4f}` | `{FINAL_RESULTS['delta_f1_vs_baseline']:+.4f}` |\\n\")\n","\n","      f.write(\"### Mitigation Strategy: Post-hoc Threshold Calibration\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"- **Calibration Target:** Recall ≥ {TARGET_RECALL} per `{mitigation_col}` group.\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"- **Methodology:** Thresholds optimized on a 20% validation split to ensure equitable treatment, then verified on a 20% unseen holdout set.\\n\\n\")\n","\n","      f.write(\"### Subgroup Calibration Details\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"| Subgroup | Calibrated Threshold | Notes |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","      for group, threshold in group_thresholds.items():\n","       f.write(f\"| {group} | `{threshold:.4f}` | Reached target recall on Val set |\\n\")\n","\n","      f.write(f\"\\n### Final Performance (Unseen Holdout Set)\\n\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| Metric | Value | Δ vs Baseline |\\n|---|---|---|\\n\")\n","      delta_auc = FINAL_RESULTS.get('delta_auc_vs_baseline', 0)\n","      f.write(f\"| AUC | `{FINAL_RESULTS['AUC']:.4f}` | `{delta_auc:+.4f}` |\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| **F1-Score** | `{FINAL_RESULTS['F1']:.4f}` | `{FINAL_RESULTS['F1'] - baseline_f1:+.4f}` |\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| **Recall (Global)** | `{FINAL_RESULTS['Recall']:.4f}` | — |\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| **Precision (Global)** | `{FINAL_RESULTS['Precision']:.4f}` | — |\\n\")\n","      f.write(f\"| **Features Used** | `{FINAL_RESULTS['n_features']}` | Strictly vetted set |\\n\\n\")\n","\n","      f.write(\"### Final Verdict\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"> The model has been successfully mitigated for fairness. By lowering thresholds for historically under-represented or under-predicted groups, we achieved a more equitable distribution of high-income predictions, with a manageable trade-off in global precision.\\n\")\n","\n","      f.write(\"\\n## Lessons Learned\\n\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"1. **Capital gain binary flag** provides outsized recall uplift vs raw continuous value.\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"2. **Married × Education interaction** is the single most important FN-reducing feature.\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"3. **Per-group threshold calibration** meaningfully closes TPR gaps at modest precision cost.\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"4. **Excluding sensitive features** does not eliminate proxy-based disparity — threshold\\n\" +\n","             \"    calibration is more effective for this dataset.\\n\")\n","      f.write(\"5. **Fold-level variance monitoring** caught unstable features early, avoiding overfitting.\\n\")\n","      print(f\"  Pipeline summary (full) → {summary_path}\")\n","      from IPython.display import Markdown\n","      display(Markdown(filename='/content/fairness_audit_summary.md'))\n","\n","\n","\n","\n","\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","metadata":{"colab":{"base_uri":"https://localhost:8080/","height":1000},"id":"514794f3","executionInfo":{"status":"ok","timestamp":1773280889628,"user_tz":-330,"elapsed":43,"user":{"displayName":"Radhika Rao","userId":"14853356881299989236"}},"outputId":"28ba0547-d666-4819-c023-56f5c798c2de"},"source":["with open('/content/pipeline_summary_full.md', 'r') as f:\n","    md_content = f.read()\n","\n","from IPython.display import Markdown\n","display(Markdown(md_content))"],"execution_count":9,"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":["<IPython.core.display.Markdown object>"],"text/markdown":"# UCI Adult Income — FeatureBot Complete Pipeline Summary\n\n**Run date:** 2026-03-12 00:28\n\n## Phase 1 — Baseline\n- AUC: `0.9200 ± 0.0025`\n- F1:  `0.6806 ± 0.0064`\n\n## Phase 2 — Template B (FN Reduction) Feature Proposals\n\n| ID | Name | FN Rationale | Leakage |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| B1 | `high_capital_gain_flag` | Captures sparse but decisive signal; model misses these because linear scaling dilutes extreme values. | PASS |\n| B2 | `exec_managerial_flag` | Reduces FN for white-collar workers whose other features (e.g., moderate hours) appear 'average'. | PASS |\n| B3 | `married_highEdu_interaction` | Interaction creates a distinct high-income profile cluster not separately captured by either feature alone. | PASS |\n| B4 | `age_edu_interaction` | Reduces FN for prime-age (35–55) professionals; raw age + edu alone underweight combined effect. | PASS |\n| B5 | `overtime_professional_flag` | Synthesises hours and role to flag the 'overworked professional' archetype that drives many >50K FNs. | PASS |\n| B6 | `private_sector_flag` | Explicit indicator helps model attend to within-private variation more carefully; baseline lumps all non-government workers. | PASS |\n\n**Best Phase B experiment:** `B_EXP04_NO_MARRIED_EDU` — AUC `0.9221`, Recall `0.6215`\n\n## Phase 3 — Fairness Diagnostics\n\n### By race\n\n| Group | n | AUC | TPR | FPR | FN_rate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Other | 406 | 0.9567 | 0.4800 | 0.0225 | 0.5200 |\n| Black | 4683 | 0.9513 | 0.5318 | 0.0192 | 0.4682 |\n| White | 41714 | 0.9218 | 0.6310 | 0.0576 | 0.3690 |\n| Amer-Indian-Eskimo | 470 | 0.9187 | 0.5818 | 0.0193 | 0.4182 |\n| Asian-Pac-Islander | 1517 | 0.9043 | 0.6626 | 0.0912 | 0.3374 |\n\n### By gender\n\n| Group | n | AUC | TPR | FPR | FN_rate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Female | 16176 | 0.9480 | 0.5523 | 0.0148 | 0.4477 |\n| Male | 32614 | 0.9055 | 0.6396 | 0.0781 | 0.3604 |\n\n### By marital_status\n\n| Group | n | AUC | TPR | FPR | FN_rate |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Never-married | 16082 | 0.9440 | 0.3752 | 0.0009 | 0.6248 |\n| Separated | 1530 | 0.9141 | 0.3333 | 0.0028 | 0.6667 |\n| Married-spouse-absent | 627 | 0.8997 | 0.3103 | 0.0018 | 0.6897 |\n| Widowed | 1518 | 0.8952 | 0.3281 | 0.0007 | 0.6719 |\n| Divorced | 6630 | 0.8862 | 0.3308 | 0.0030 | 0.6692 |\n| Married-civ-spouse | 22366 | 0.8510 | 0.6736 | 0.1572 | 0.3264 |\n| Married-AF-spouse | 37 | 0.8307 | 0.4286 | 0.0435 | 0.5714 |\n\n\n────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n## PHASE 4 — FINAL CONSOLIDATED EVALUATION (60/20/20)\n\n| Metric | Value | Δ vs Baseline |\n|---|---|---|\n| AUC | `0.9168` | `-0.0033` |\n| F1 | `0.6996` | `+0.0190` |\n### Mitigation Strategy: Post-hoc Threshold Calibration\n- **Calibration Target:** Recall ≥ 0.7 per `race` group.\n- **Methodology:** Thresholds optimized on a 20% validation split to ensure equitable treatment, then verified on a 20% unseen holdout set.\n\n### Subgroup Calibration Details\n| Subgroup | Calibrated Threshold | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Black | `0.3132` | Reached target recall on Val set |\n| White | `0.4137` | Reached target recall on Val set |\n| Asian-Pac-Islander | `0.3562` | Reached target recall on Val set |\n| Amer-Indian-Eskimo | `0.4529` | Reached target recall on Val set |\n| Other | `0.3056` | Reached target recall on Val set |\n\n### Final Performance (Unseen Holdout Set)\n\n| Metric | Value | Δ vs Baseline |\n|---|---|---|\n| AUC | `0.9168` | `-0.0033` |\n| **F1-Score** | `0.6996` | `+0.0190` |\n| **Recall (Global)** | `0.6965` | — |\n| **Precision (Global)** | `0.7028` | — |\n| **Features Used** | `25` | Strictly vetted set |\n\n### Final Verdict\n> The model has been successfully mitigated for fairness. By lowering thresholds for historically under-represented or under-predicted groups, we achieved a more equitable distribution of high-income predictions, with a manageable trade-off in global precision.\n\n## Lessons Learned\n\n1. **Capital gain binary flag** provides outsized recall uplift vs raw continuous value.\n2. **Married × Education interaction** is the single most important FN-reducing feature.\n3. **Per-group threshold calibration** meaningfully closes TPR gaps at modest precision cost.\n4. **Excluding sensitive features** does not eliminate proxy-based disparity — threshold\n    calibration is more effective for this dataset.\n5. **Fold-level varia